# E021's Session A step blocks, in the E002 step language (runtime/iwp/spike/steps.py), run one
# step at a time through the session (Session.perform) by runtime/iwp/driver/clicks.py. The loop
# (e021_loop.py) composes these blocks with the attack flow's own synthesised clicks -- select the
# attacker, ATTACK, the target, the attacker again, one exchange, QUIT ATTACK / DONE -- which it
# sends through the same click-driver, one step at a time, so no input leaves the driver's
# accounting. Coordinates are the 800x600 stage's (walkthroughs/coordinates.md). A block starts at
# a "# --- block NAME" line and runs to the next one. The block texts of new-game, quiet, dismiss
# and the three notices are E020's own (experiments/E020-wine-first-run/play.steps), unchanged:
# their coordinates are measured, and E020's rules (New Game from the title only, T41) hold here.

# --- block new-game
# From the title screen only (T41): the order and the points are E002's loss-easy.steps (New Game,
# EASY, Play Game). The loop never sends this block from a board: New Game in the middle of a live
# game quits it, and with the human holding fewer than 10 countries the game credits a loss, writes
# its scoreboard file and shows the Scoreboard (F003; sitting 20261008T204817Z). EASY is a plain
# click: the setup screen of a later game may already show EASY. The computers' first turns follow
# (block quiet).
watch all
click! 100 585
settle
click 533 311
click! 565 532

# --- block quiet
# The computers' turns: the board unchanged for 4 s (a poll on the screen, bounded by the spike).
# F003: 15 to 33 s before the first human turn, 23 to 24 s after a pass. The loop repeats this
# block until the board is quiet or its attempts are spent.
watch 0 0 800 495
settle 4

# --- block place-commit
# ALL, then PLACE: every reinforcement goes on the one country the loop selected before this block
# (the placement row only lights for a country the human owns; the selection is the loop's
# synthesised `click-until?` on that country's point, with E020's own placement-row test). The
# ATTACK phase follows; PASS is block pass.
watch 262 502 276 70
click! 307 543
click! 497 543
settle

# --- block pass
# PASS, then CONTINUE when a card was awarded (E020's commit block, split: the Session A turn
# attacks between the placement and the pass). Sent once the attack phase is over and the turn is
# still the human's.
watch 262 502 276 70
click! 417 530
click-any? 402 531

# --- block dismiss
# A prompt between turns (a card or an event message) that keeps the placement row from showing:
# CONTINUE when it is there; the loop then waits for a quiet board and tries the placement again.
watch 262 502 276 70
click-any? 402 531

# --- block eliminated-keep-playing
# The elimination notice (runtime/iwp/driver/screens.py `eliminated`): of its two buttons in the
# bottom bar, the one that lets the computers play the game out, red, centre 665,531. The owner's
# decision (T38 round 4): keep playing. Sent once; the notice must go (the screen changes).
watch all
click! 665 531

# --- block game-over-continue
# The winner notice (runtime/iwp/driver/screens.py `game-over`): its one grey CONTINUE button in
# the middle of the bottom bar, centre 401,534. Sent once, after the loop has logged the game's
# end; the notice must go (the screen changes). What follows is read from the screen, never
# assumed: the next game starts only on the title.
watch all
click! 401 534

# --- block scoreboard-continue
# The Scoreboard (runtime/iwp/driver/screens.py `scoreboard`): shown after the game credits a
# loss, with one grey CONTINUE button in the bottom bar, centre 401,526. Sent once, after the
# loop has logged `loss-credited`; the screen must change. The next game starts only on the title.
watch all
click! 401 526
